            <div xml:id="d365">

                <pb facs="0491" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg406"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72113/1102: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jones</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tegucigalpa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-23T12:00:00-05:48"><hi rendition="#italic">August 23,
                                1919, noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received August
                            26, 6.14 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram July 17, 7 p.m. and July 29, 5 p.m. President Bertrand
                    informed me last night that the Supreme Court rendered <pb facs="0492" n="407"
                        xml:id="pg407"/> decision denying the right of <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >amparo</hi> to the Germans and that he instructed Alien Property Custodian
                    to proceed with all vigor, disregarding German claims and protests.</p>
                <p>He asks that you send him copies of treaty of peace with Germany.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jones</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
